{"parentUuid":"08ab4394-6206-4e59-9735-b8efcd9ca109","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011QFG7bs4a9pNWXEyhJB8A7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q24H8s4Bu6istuKLPrNbYK","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"ShinkaEvolve evolutionary code optimization framework 2026"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7298,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":329,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7298},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":329,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7298,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7298,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyShmrEv335WdUHaUep","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ed0d70a5-406f-47f5-98f6-70b8cd14b1e7","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:40.910Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"57564d33-3324-4527-983a-8444c24299be","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fq3L9MCExT3ai2u1unHCPj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AlphaEvolve SEARCH REPLACE block code evolution prompt format\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Google’s AlphaEvolve: Getting Started with Evolutionary Coding Agents | Towards Data Science\",\"url\":\"https://towardsdatascience.com/googles-alphaevolve-getting-started-with-evolutionary-coding-agents/\"},{\"title\":\"[Literature Review] AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://www.themoonlight.io/en/review/alphaevolve-a-coding-agent-for-scientific-and-algorithmic-discovery\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"OpenEvolve: An Open Source Implementation of Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/codelion/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve | cbarkinozer | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://cbarkinozer.medium.com/alphaevolve-419242a0a4b4\"},{\"title\":\"CodeEvolve: An open source evolutionary coding agent for algorithm discovery and optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14150v2\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A Gemini-powered coding agent for designing advanced algorithms — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: Evolutionary agent from DeepMind - Composio\",\"url\":\"https://composio.dev/blog/alphaevolve-evolutionary-agent-from-deepmind\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaEvolve: A coding agent for scientific and algorithmic discovery\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/AlphaEvolve.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"alphaevolve - by Michael Eliot - Important Works\",\"url\":\"https://importantworks.substack.com/p/alphaevolve\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found detailed information about AlphaEvolve's SEARCH REPLACE block code evolution prompt format:\n\n## AlphaEvolve SEARCH REPLACE Block Format\n\nThe LLM is instructed to use a diff output format: `<<<<<<< SEARCH search text ======= replace text >>>>>>> REPLACE`\n\n### How It Works\n\nThe LLM's output is a list of code sequences that the LLM wants replaced, meaning the LLM does not have to reproduce the entire program but can instead trigger modifications to specific lines. This presumably allows AlphaEvolve to handle larger code bases more efficiently.\n\n### Code Evolution Blocks\n\nAlphaEvolve supports marking specific code blocks within a larger codebase using comments (`# EVOLVE-BLOCK-START` and `# EVOLVE-BLOCK-END`). The initial code within these blocks serves as the starting point, and the surrounding code provides necessary infrastructure for evaluation.\n\n### Format Details\n\nThe LLM modifies the parent's code according to a diff-based SEARCH/REPLACE format, where the LLM first searches for a specific section of code, and then replaces it with the proposed modifications, ensuring targeted and precise edits.\n\nThis structured format allows AlphaEvolve to make precise, surgical modifications to code during the evolutionary process without needing to regenerate entire files.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"921c54f2-1ecf-4941-9e77-b47f36c5c58d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:46.872Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"57564d33-3324-4527-983a-8444c24299be","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"ed0d70a5-406f-47f5-98f6-70b8cd14b1e7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q24H8s4Bu6istuKLPrNbYK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ShinkaEvolve evolutionary code optimization framework 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - SakanaAI/ShinkaEvolve: ShinkaEvolve: Towards Open-Ended and Sample-Efficient Program Evolution 🧬\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/SakanaAI/ShinkaEvolve\"},{\"title\":\"ShinkaEvolve: Evolving New Algorithms with LLMs, Orders of Magnitude More Efficiently\",\"url\":\"https://sakana.ai/shinka-evolve/\"},{\"title\":\"ShinkaEvolve: Towards Open-Ended And Sample-Efficient ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.19349\"},{\"title\":\"ShinkaEvolve: Towards Open-Ended And Sample-Efficient Program Evolution\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.19349v1\"},{\"title\":\"[2509.19349] ShinkaEvolve: Towards Open-Ended And Sample-Efficient Program Evolution\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.19349\"},{\"title\":\"ShinkaEvolve: Towards Open-Ended and Sample-Efficient Program Evolution | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=lKEdGCoDNC\"},{\"title\":\"Ch 6. ShinkaEvolve - Evolutionary AI Survey\",\"url\":\"https://evo.si5.pl/chapters/shinkaevolve.html\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR Poster ShinkaEvolve: Towards Open-Ended and Sample-Efficient Program Evolution\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/virtual/2026/poster/10007692\"},{\"title\":\"CODEEVOLVE: an open-source evolutionary framework for\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.14150\"},{\"title\":\"CodeEvolve: an open-source evolutionary framework for algorithmic discovery and optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14150v4\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's comprehensive information about ShinkaEvolve:\n\n## Overview\n\nShinkaEvolve is an evolutionary code optimization framework which discovers new algorithms with LLMs and achieves unprecedented sample efficiency. The Japanese word 'Shinka' (進化) means 'evolution' or 'gradual development'.\n\n## Key Features and Innovations\n\nShinkaEvolve substantially improves sample efficiency through three key algorithmic innovations: a novel parent program sampling strategy, code novelty rejection-sampling, and adaptive performance-based LLM ensemble selection. \n\nBy leveraging the creative capabilities of LLMs and the optimization power of evolutionary search, ShinkaEvolve enables automated exploration and improvement of scientific code.\n\n## Recent Developments in 2026\n\nIn January 2026, ShinkaEvolve was accepted at ICLR 2026 and an update with new features was released. In April 2026, a new documentation website was added with guides for getting started, configuration, async evolution, local models, WebUI usage, and agentic workflows. In May 2026, Headless CLI-backed mutation models were added for subscription-backed agent usage.\n\n## Practical Performance\n\nShinkaEvolve discovered a new state-of-the-art solution for the classic 26-circle packing problem using only 150 samples. This represents a significant efficiency improvement compared to previous approaches.\n\n## Open Source and Accessibility\n\nShinkaEvolve is an open-source framework (Apache 2.0 License) designed from the ground up to tackle the critical limitations of existing approaches: poor sample efficiency and their closed-source nature.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ec55284b-7046-4bdf-a8f1-5311a9db7200","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:48.188Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ed0d70a5-406f-47f5-98f6-70b8cd14b1e7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"08ab4394-6206-4e59-9735-b8efcd9ca109","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AyJkLgfHbDQi2v23Ga3fDt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OpenEvolve github configuration LLM evaluator yaml example\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - celerycelery/openevolve: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/celerycelery/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - SuperCodeTool/OpenEvolving: Open-source implementation of AlphaEvolve · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/SuperCodeTool/OpenEvolving\"},{\"title\":\"OpenEvolve: Teaching LLMs to Discover Algorithms Through Evolution - Algorithmic SuperIntelligence Labs\",\"url\":\"https://algorithmicsuperintelligence.ai/blog/openevolve-overview/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"openevolve · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/openevolve/0.2.4/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - WarrenZhu050413/openevolve-writing: Fork of OpenEvolve, focused on Writing · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/WarrenZhu050413/openevolve-writing\"},{\"title\":\"Beyond Code Generation: Continuously Evolve Text with LLMs | Towards Data Science\",\"url\":\"https://towardsdatascience.com/beyond-code-generation-continuously-evolve-text-with-llms/\"},{\"title\":\"[Question]LLM prompt evolution optimisation with feedback · Issue #315 · algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve/issues/315\"},{\"title\":\"OpenEvolve: An Open Source Implementation of Google DeepMind's AlphaEvolve\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/blog/codelion/openevolve\"},{\"title\":\"Suggestion on LLM models config in config.yaml · Issue #160 · algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/codelion/openevolve/issues/160\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OpenEvolve configuration and LLM evaluator YAML examples:\n\n## Configuration Overview\n\nOpenEvolve uses configuration files in YAML format to specify settings like LLM models, evolution strategies, and evaluation parameters.\n\n## Example YAML Configuration\n\nHere's an example configuration structure found in the documentation:\n\nAn advanced configuration example includes settings for max_iterations, random_seed, LLM models with ensemble configuration including multiple model names and weights, temperature settings, database configuration with population_size and num_islands, and evaluator settings with enable_artifacts, cascade_evaluation, and use_llm_feedback options.\n\nA more basic example shows: `max_iterations: 1000`, `llm` section with `primary_model: \"gemini-2.0-flash-lite\"`, `secondary_model: \"gemini-2.0-flash\"`, `temperature: 0.7`, and `database` settings with `population_size: 500` and `num_islands: 5`.\n\n## Evaluator Configuration\n\nFor the evaluator component, the configuration can include `enable_artifacts: true` to enable error feedback, `cascade_evaluation: true` for multi-stage testing, `use_llm_feedback: true` for AI code quality assessment, and settings for including artifacts in prompts.\n\nThe official OpenEvolve repositories on GitHub contain complete working examples in the `examples/` directory, including configuration files that demonstrate these settings in practice.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4b37064a-9f9f-45c2-8b05-922b6e931d94","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:50.936Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"08ab4394-6206-4e59-9735-b8efcd9ca109","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4ecbe89b-47d0-49f0-93eb-012db7082c4b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HKXRrzEjYQo2tybiPErShK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"FunSearch DeepMind bin packing prompt evaluator code structure\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-deepmind/funsearch · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/funsearch\"},{\"title\":\"funsearch/bin_packing/bin_packing.ipynb at main · google-deepmind/funsearch\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/funsearch/blob/main/bin_packing/bin_packing.ipynb\"},{\"title\":\"This is the author’s version of the work accepted in Nature.\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/Mathematical-discoveries-from-program-search-with-large-language-models.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"FunSearch: Making new discoveries in mathematical sciences using Large Language Models - Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/discover/blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/\"},{\"title\":\"FunSearch: Making new discoveries in mathematical sciences using Large Language Models — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/\"},{\"title\":\"Implement FunSearch in DSPy · Issue #253 · stanfordnlp/dspy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/stanfordnlp/dspy/issues/253\"},{\"title\":\"Mathematical discoveries from program search with large language models | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06924-6\"},{\"title\":\"Google DeepMind announces the \\\"FunSearch\\\" training method\",\"url\":\"https://www.gizchina.com/2023/12/15/google-deepmind-funsearch-method-mathematics-computer-science/\"},{\"title\":\"Core Implementation | google-deepmind/funsearch | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google-deepmind/funsearch/2-core-implementation\"},{\"title\":\"Inside FunSearch: Google DeepMind’s New LLM that is Able to Discover New Math and Computer Science Algorithms | Towards AI\",\"url\":\"https://towardsai.net/p/artificial-intelligence/inside-funsearch-google-deepminds-new-llm-that-is-able-to-discover-new-math-and-computer-science-algorithms\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide you with information about FunSearch's bin packing implementation and evaluator code structure:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe bin_packing module contains heuristics discovered by FunSearch for online 1D bin packing problems, and an evaluation suite to reproduce the results reported in the paper.\n\n## Core Architecture\n\nThe input to FunSearch is a specification of the problem in the form of an evaluate function, an initial implementation of the function to evolve, which can be trivial, and potentially a skeleton. The user writes a description of the problem in the form of code, comprising a procedure to evaluate programs, and a seed program used to initialize a pool of programs.\n\n## Code Structure Components\n\nFunSearch's implementation has four primary components:\n\n1. **ProgramsDatabase**: Maintains the history of successful programs discovered during the evolutionary process and stores evolved functions along with their performance metrics.\n\n2. **Evaluator**: The Evaluator class analyzes functions generated by language models to determine their effectiveness and compiles candidate functions into executable programs.\n\n3. **Sampler**: Handles the generation of candidate functions, creates prompts based on the best-performing programs from the database, interacts with language models to generate candidate code snippets, and submits generated candidates to evaluators.\n\n## Evolutionary Process\n\nAt each iteration, FunSearch builds a prompt by combining several programs sampled from the programs database (favouring high-scoring ones), the prompt is then fed to the pre-trained LLM, and new programs are created. Newly created programs are then scored and stored in the programs database (if correct).\n\n## Availability\n\nThe discovered functions as well as the evolutionary algorithm, code manipulation routines and a single-threaded implementation of the FunSearch pipeline are available as Python code in the Supplementary Information and at https://github.com/google-deepmind/funsearch.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"f0baf116-9f82-4b1f-a7d8-5584bdef40e3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:10:51.777Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4ecbe89b-47d0-49f0-93eb-012db7082c4b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
