{"parentUuid":"3bc1dae5-7a53-493a-ba8e-2309c2621dec","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bjf38YkM1LMF7xzycqoB25","type":"tool_result","content":"I appreciate your detailed request, but I cannot extract the specific technical information you're asking for because the webpage content provided only shows GitHub's navigation interface and file metadata for `bin_packing.ipynb`. \n\nThe actual Jupyter notebook content—including the evaluate function structure, seed program, prompt template, metrics, and filtering logic—is not included in the provided text. The page displays \"438 lines (438 loc) · 154 KB\" but the substantive code and documentation content isn't rendered in what was shared.\n\nTo answer your questions accurately, I would need:\n- The actual notebook cells showing the evaluation framework\n- The initialization code with the priority function\n- The prompt engineering template being used\n- The metric collection and logging code\n- The validation/filtering mechanisms\n\nI recommend accessing the raw notebook directly via the GitHub raw file link or cloning the repository to examine the full implementation details."}]},"uuid":"9bcaf4b1-0b13-488e-aebb-1eb2df43c847","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:01.726Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3bc1dae5-7a53-493a-ba8e-2309c2621dec","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f67c0489-98da-4a2e-a0af-784e8c5f6da5","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DmkrmfJxeq2NtyWcoVv1Kg","type":"tool_result","content":"# OpenEvolve Project Structure & Technical Details\n\n## 1. Directory Structure\n\nBased on the repository layout shown:\n\n```\nopenevolve/\n├── .github/\n├── configs/\n├── examples/\n│   ├── function_minimization/\n│   ├── mlx_metal_kernel_opt/\n│   ├── rust_adaptive_sort/\n│   ├── symbolic_regression/\n│   └── circle_packing/\n├── openevolve/          (main package)\n├── scripts/\n├── tests/\n├── .gitignore\n├── Dockerfile\n├── pyproject.toml\n├── setup.py\n└── openevolve-run.py    (CLI entry point)\n```\n\n## 2. Evaluator Function Signature\n\nThe documentation shows evaluators should return a dictionary with metrics:\n\n```python\nevaluator = lambda path: {\"score\": benchmark_result}\n```\n\nOr using the `EvaluationResult` class with artifacts:\n\n```python\nreturn EvaluationResult(\n    metrics={\"performance\": 0.85, \"correctness\": 1.0},\n    artifacts={...}\n)\n```\n\n**Expected dictionary keys**: `performance`, `correctness`, `combined_score`, or custom metric names.\n\n## 3. EVOLVE-BLOCK Markers\n\nThe content does not explicitly document EVOLVE-BLOCK marker syntax for `initial_program.py`. This detail is absent from the provided documentation.\n\n## 4. Config.yaml Schema (Cascade Evaluation & LLM Feedback)\n\nRelevant configuration sections mentioned:\n\n```yaml\nevaluator:\n  enable_artifacts: true      # Error feedback to LLM\n  cascade_evaluation: true    # Multi-stage testing\n  use_llm_feedback: true      # AI code quality assessment\n\nllm:\n  models:\n    - name: \"model-name\"\n      weight: 0.6\n  temperature: 0.7\n```\n\n## 5. Command-Line Entry Point\n\n```bash\npython openevolve-run.py <initial_program.py> <evaluator.py> \\\n  --config <config.yaml> --iterations <N>\n```"}]},"uuid":"5942c544-2327-4fb5-b83e-cb896a1e7a26","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:05.195Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f67c0489-98da-4a2e-a0af-784e8c5f6da5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"50f44629-636e-422c-a20e-0cb9ffd31444","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YCjjf8eC8ojiaVWtd2LtxB","type":"tool_result","content":"# ShinkaEvolve Analysis\n\nBased on the provided GitHub documentation, here are the requested details:\n\n## 1) ShinkaEvolve vs. OpenEvolve Evaluator Interface\nThe page does not contain a direct comparison between ShinkaEvolve and OpenEvolve's evaluator interfaces. It only mentions OpenEvolve as a \"related open-source project\" without technical comparison details.\n\n## 2) Novelty Rejection-Sampling Mechanism\nThe documentation references a novelty system with these parameters: `\"max_novelty_attempts\": 3` and `\"code_embed_sim_threshold\": 0.99`. The mechanism uses code embeddings to filter similar solutions, but the exact rejection-sampling algorithm is not detailed in this content.\n\n## 3) Parent Sampling Strategy\nThe framework supports multiple approaches: `\"parent_selection_strategy\"` can be `\"weighted\"`, `\"power_law\"`, or `\"beam_search\"`. The weighted strategy uses `\"exploitation_alpha\": 1.0` (power-law exponent) and `\"parent_selection_lambda\": 10.0` (sigmoid sharpness). An `\"exploitation_ratio\": 0.2` controls archive sampling probability.\n\n## 4) Example Task Definitions\nThe page lists several built-in examples including circle packing optimization, Game 2048 policy optimization, Julia prime-counting solvers, and Fortran heat diffusion stencils. Each uses `LocalJobConfig` for execution.\n\n## 5) System Prompt Template\nThe default system message is: *\"You are an expert optimization and algorithm design assistant. Improve the program while preserving correctness and immutable regions.\"* This can be customized via the `task_sys_msg` configuration parameter."}]},"uuid":"06e092b3-59d7-41ec-9767-bcb502bba18b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:07.815Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"50f44629-636e-422c-a20e-0cb9ffd31444","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
