{"parentUuid":"15c86aa3-6516-4094-af9c-3bae54ccf516","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011ozQGQd4C2HCg1vmhxcbQw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011HREEU73DV5dL8ubcZLmKe","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/googles-alphaevolve-getting-started-with-evolutionary-coding-agents/","prompt":"Extract: full prompt template structure for AlphaEvolve, what context is included (parent program, score history, inspiration programs), how SEARCH/REPLACE diff is formatted in actual prompts, and what the system prompt instructs."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6249,"cache_read_input_tokens":22296,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6249,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyVAitjKdueXGoZkCVp","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"fce806ec-1080-435c-9686-efd8a98df21b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:16.273Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fce806ec-1080-435c-9686-efd8a98df21b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011ozQGQd4C2HCg1vmhxcbQw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qq89AsPRAevK1RNubYeRbS","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://algorithmicsuperintelligence.ai/blog/openevolve-overview/index.html","prompt":"Extract: the full lifecycle of one iteration, EVOLVE-BLOCK syntax with example, cascade evaluator structure (stage1/stage2/stage3), how artifacts are surfaced to next prompt, MAP-Elites or island-based population details, common failure modes mentioned."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6249,"cache_read_input_tokens":22296,"output_tokens":570,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6249},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":570,"cache_read_input_tokens":22296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6249,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6249,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyVAitjKdueXGoZkCVp","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b5cc8c04-790b-4473-82e0-c7c4c53fb7ba","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:18.114Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"15c86aa3-6516-4094-af9c-3bae54ccf516","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016rhNNhkRMtCUuKuQXqnsU3","type":"tool_result","content":"# Bin Packing Heuristics - FunSearch Implementation\n\nBased on the notebook content, here's what I can extract about the FunSearch framework for bin packing:\n\n## Key Components\n\n**Priority Function Structure:**\nThe skeleton implements a priority-based heuristic where items are assigned to bins based on calculated priority scores. The function takes item sizes and bin capacities as inputs to generate ordering decisions.\n\n**Evaluation Function:**\nThe evaluation process measures heuristic performance by:\n- Running the packing algorithm on provided instances\n- Counting total bins used\n- Comparing against theoretical lower bounds (L1 bound calculation)\n- Computing performance metrics across multiple test cases\n\n**Decorator Pattern:**\nThe framework uses two primary decorators:\n- `@funsearch.run` - initiates the search process\n- `@funsearch.evolve` - enables evolutionary optimization of candidate solutions\n\n**Metrics Computed:**\n- Number of bins required per instance\n- Ratio against lower bounds\n- Aggregate performance across OR3 dataset (20 instances, 500 items each)\n- Performance on Weibull 5k instances (5 instances, 5,000 items each)\n- Capacity constraints (bin sizes: 150 for OR3, 100 for Weibull)\n\nThe implementation discovers heuristics by evolving priority functions that minimize bin usage while respecting problem constraints."}]},"uuid":"66400df8-a905-4165-a57f-60f4e272142c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:19.531Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"15c86aa3-6516-4094-af9c-3bae54ccf516","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"fce806ec-1080-435c-9686-efd8a98df21b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011HREEU73DV5dL8ubcZLmKe","type":"tool_result","content":"# AlphaEvolve Prompt Template Structure\n\nBased on the article, here's what's documented about the prompt architecture:\n\n## Context Components Included\n\nThe LLM receives evolutionary context containing:\n- **Successful and unsuccessful past code attempts** with their performance history\n- **Fitness feedback** showing program strengths and weaknesses across metrics\n- **Human instructions** for the specific problem being solved\n- **Meta-prompts**: self-managed instructions that evolve alongside the code\n- **Elite candidate solutions** mixed with ordinary ones for diversity\n\n## SEARCH/REPLACE Diff Format\n\nThe article specifies the exact format the LLM uses for code modifications:\n\n```\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\nsearch text\n=======\nreplace text\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```\n\nThis allows the LLM to \"target modifications to specific lines\" rather than regenerating entire programs, improving efficiency with larger codebases.\n\n## System Prompt Instruction\n\nThe framework instructs LLMs through system prompts. The article provides an example:\n\n\"You are an expert programmer specializing in tricky code problems. Your task is to find a function that returns an integer that matches an unknown, but trivial requirement.\"\n\nThe article notes this prompt demonstrates how the agent explores solution space intelligently, attempting progressively better approaches based on feedback."}]},"uuid":"2bf76cae-f613-48e7-b79b-e4f530f9e40c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:22.810Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fce806ec-1080-435c-9686-efd8a98df21b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b5cc8c04-790b-4473-82e0-c7c4c53fb7ba","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qq89AsPRAevK1RNubYeRbS","type":"tool_result","content":"# OpenEvolve: System Mechanics & Lifecycle\n\n## Full Iteration Lifecycle\n\nEach evolution cycle follows this sequence:\n\n1. **Prompt Construction**: The Prompt Sampler selects a parent program and curates evidence (top performers, ancestors, diverse extremes, random samples) with execution context.\n\n2. **Code Generation**: The LLM Ensemble generates candidate implementations using weighted model selection and configured generation parameters.\n\n3. **Evaluation**: The Evaluator executes the program with timeouts, optionally applying staged filtering, and captures execution artifacts.\n\n4. **Population Update**: The Program Database applies MAP-Elites logic, accepting candidates that improve fitness within feature bins.\n\n5. **Migration**: When per-island generation thresholds are met, top programs transfer across islands via ring topology.\n\n6. **Termination Check**: The Controller assesses stopping criteria before scheduling the next iteration.\n\n## EVOLVE-BLOCK Syntax\n\nThe document mentions two primary edit modes but doesn't formally specify \"EVOLVE-BLOCK\" syntax. Instead, it references:\n\n- **Diff-based editing** (default): Uses \"SEARCH/REPLACE blocks\"\n- **Full rewrites**: JSON or code-block extraction from LLM responses\n\n## Cascade Evaluator Structure\n\nThe three-stage pipeline operates as follows:\n\n- **Stage 1**: Fast checks (imports, execution validation)\n- **Stage 2**: Lightweight test suites\n- **Stage 3**: Comprehensive benchmarks\n\n\"Candidates must meet stage thresholds to advance.\" Timeouts and exceptions become artifacts for feedback.\n\n## Artifact Surfacing\n\nThe \"artifact side-channel\" mechanism captures stderr, tracebacks, and execution traces, which are \"fed back into subsequent prompts,\" allowing the LLM to learn from failures contextually.\n\n## MAP-Elites & Islands\n\nEach island maintains a MAP-Elites grid with configurable feature dimensions (complexity, diversity, custom evaluator-supplied metrics). Candidates occupy cells if they improve fitness; one elite per cell is enforced. Migration occurs \"event-driven\" when generation counts reach thresholds, not wall-clock time, using ring topology by default.\n\n## Mentioned Failure Modes\n\nThe document does not explicitly enumerate common failure modes."}]},"uuid":"196eb6e8-4726-4d85-848b-94ad26167597","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:26.810Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b5cc8c04-790b-4473-82e0-c7c4c53fb7ba","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
