{"parentUuid":"cb65d907-7a60-4dbe-830d-d59926efc656","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CR8fT2Aekygx3xm83Tz7BB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J3osu9WA8v43tsru646zVD","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.19349v1","prompt":"Extract: ShinkaEvolve novelty rejection-sampling algorithm details, parent sampling power-law / sigmoid formula, the prompt template / structure, what metrics evaluators must return, and any failure modes / safeguards mentioned (reward hacking, invalid code)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2390,"cache_read_input_tokens":28545,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2390,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":60,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyWZyQcchmrrPUyjREi","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f756c912-d746-449f-a6c0-f440fc34f73d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:34.861Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f756c912-d746-449f-a6c0-f440fc34f73d","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CR8fT2Aekygx3xm83Tz7BB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012GpHsR3ewHmnPc36nvuUc4","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"FunSearch evolve cut MILP cutting plane LLM heuristic discovery"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2390,"cache_read_input_tokens":28545,"output_tokens":439,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2390},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":439,"cache_read_input_tokens":28545,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2390,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2390,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyWZyQcchmrrPUyjREi","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"098b15ae-d3b5-48e9-9327-aa58d65472ce","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:36.001Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cb65d907-7a60-4dbe-830d-d59926efc656","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ac68b9dc-9847-4e6f-8ec2-6b4367414408","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XAS9MN7SVQGpAfkwiJjVvX","type":"tool_result","content":"# EVOLVE-BLOCK Syntax\n\nThe evolution block uses comment markers to delineate code eligible for optimization:\n\n```python\n# EVOLVE-BLOCK-START\n\n\"\"\"Constructor-based circle packing for n=26 circles\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct a specific arrangement of 26 circles in a unit square\n    that attempts to maximize the sum of their radii.\n    ...\n    \"\"\"\n    # [function body with circle placement logic]\n    return centers, radii, sum_radii\n\ndef compute_max_radii(centers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compute the maximum possible radii for each circle position\n    ...\n    \"\"\"\n    # [function implementation]\n    return radii\n\n# EVOLVE-BLOCK-END\n```\n\n**Key structure:**\n- Opening marker: `# EVOLVE-BLOCK-START` \n- Closing marker: `# EVOLVE-BLOCK-END`\n- All code between these comments is subject to evolutionary optimization\n- Both complete functions (`construct_packing` and `compute_max_radii`) fall within the block\n- The comment notes that code outside this block \"remains fixed (not evolved)\""}]},"uuid":"45c84288-e9a6-40ac-a7ee-388d69ada9ae","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:37.458Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cb65d907-7a60-4dbe-830d-d59926efc656","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"098b15ae-d3b5-48e9-9327-aa58d65472ce","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d8b963fa-dadc-413b-9392-667bd1294b0d","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012GpHsR3ewHmnPc36nvuUc4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"FunSearch evolve cut MILP cutting plane LLM heuristic discovery\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"EvoCut: Strengthening Integer Programs via Evolution Guided Language Models\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2508.11850\"},{\"title\":\"This is the author’s version of the work accepted in Nature.\",\"url\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/Mathematical-discoveries-from-program-search-with-large-language-models.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"LLMs for Cold-Start Cutting Plane Separator Configuration\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.12038v1\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Mathematical discoveries from program search with large language models\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/376546904_Mathematical_discoveries_from_program_search_with_large_language_models\"},{\"title\":\"Mathematical discoveries from program search with large language models | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06924-6\"},{\"title\":\"1 Introduction\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.12038\"},{\"title\":\"FunSearch: Making new discoveries in mathematical sciences using Large Language Models — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/\"},{\"title\":\"Evolutionary Computation in the Era of Large Language Model: Survey and Roadmap\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2401.10034v1\"},{\"title\":\"Algorithm Discovery With LLMs: Evolutionary Search Meets Reinforcement Learning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2504.05108v4\"},{\"title\":\"LARGE LANGUAGE MODELS FOR COMBINATORIAL OPTIMIZATION: A SYSTEMATIC REVIEW\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.03637\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about your query:\n\n## EvoCut: Strengthening Integer Programs via Evolution Guided Language Models\n\nThe search results reveal a recent paper titled \"EvoCut, an evolutionary algorithm powered by multiple LLM agents to iteratively generate and refine acceleration cuts that speed up solving across instances of a given MILP model.\"\n\n### Connection to FunSearch\n\nFunSearch couples a frozen LLM with evolutionary search and an evaluator to discover heuristics, while the evolution of heuristics refines natural language \"thoughts\" and executable code using evolutionary strategies. EvoCut applies this FunSearch-inspired approach specifically to the problem of discovering cutting planes for MILP solvers.\n\n### Key Features of EvoCut\n\nGiven a symbolic MILP, EvoCut automatically proposes, experimentally verifies, and evolves such cuts to improve solve time. The approach distinguishes between general-purpose cuts used by default in modern solvers and acceleration cuts tailored to a specific problem class that exploit structure in a given formulation and can yield larger speedups when designed and checked carefully.\n\n### Research Impact\n\nThe paper appears to be from February 2026 and represents an advancement in using LLMs for combinatorial optimization, particularly in automating the discovery of problem-specific cutting planes—a traditionally manual and expert-driven task in mathematical optimization.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7da0c014-aa3e-4f22-9091-4442a604c9dd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:42.803Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"098b15ae-d3b5-48e9-9327-aa58d65472ce","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"f756c912-d746-449f-a6c0-f440fc34f73d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d8b963fa-dadc-413b-9392-667bd1294b0d","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J3osu9WA8v43tsru646zVD","type":"tool_result","content":"# ShinkaEvolve: Key Technical Components\n\n## Novelty Rejection-Sampling Algorithm\n\nShinkaEvolve implements a two-stage filtering mechanism. First, it \"embed[s] mutable parts of the program code\" and \"compute[s] cosine similarity scores across the island subpopulation.\" If the maximum similarity score exceeds a threshold (η=0.95), the system \"query[ies] an LLM to further assess whether the program is meaningfully different.\" This dual approach combines embedding-based filtering with semantic validation to prevent redundant mutations.\n\n## Parent Sampling Strategies\n\nThe framework offers two contrasting approaches:\n\n**Power-Law Sampling:** Programs are ranked by fitness with selection probability following: p_i = r_i^(-α) / Σ r_j^(-α), where α controls exploitation intensity (α=0 yields uniform sampling; α→∞ implements hill-climbing).\n\n**Weighted Sampling:** Combines performance via sigmoid scaling s_i = σ(λ·(F(P_i)−α_0)) with novelty weighting h_i = 1/(1+N(P_i)), producing final probability p_i = w_i/Σw_j where w_i = s_i·h_i.\n\n## Prompt Template Structure\n\nThe framework employs a standardized format including:\n- Current program code with evolution blocks marked\n- Performance metrics and textual feedback\n- Task description and instructions\n- Explicit guidance: \"Do not rewrite the entire program - focus on targeted improvements\"\n\n## Required Evaluator Metrics\n\nEvaluators must return a dictionary containing:\n- **combined_score** (float): Primary fitness value\n- **public** (dict): Visible metrics for LLM context\n- **text_feedback** (str): Descriptive performance insights\n- **private** (dict): Hidden evaluation data\n- **extra_data** (dict): Pickled supplementary information\n\n## Failure Modes & Safeguards\n\n**Invalid Code Protection:** If LLM proposals violate immutable code constraints, the system \"resample[s] a new proposal,\" providing \"parsing feedback using Reflexion.\"\n\n**Reward Hacking Prevention:** The adaptive LLM sampling uses relative improvement r_i^u = exp(max(r_i−r_i^b, 0))−1, where r_i^b represents \"the maximum between its parent program and the initial program,\" ensuring agents \"account for the non-stationarity.\"\n\n**Search Space Constraints:** Embedding-based rejection sampling prevents near-duplicate mutations with marginal computational overhead, while meta-scratchpad systems provide \"high-level guidance from accumulated evolutionary experience\" to maintain coherent search direction."}]},"uuid":"a84dbe96-78ff-410a-a002-40170bed858e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:44.853Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f756c912-d746-449f-a6c0-f440fc34f73d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a84dbe96-78ff-410a-a002-40170bed858e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015nLSD25oxoeEHa9QUhqSNu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent — found the key piece on evolving cuts. Let me dig into EvoCut and one more piece on failure modes."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1269,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1788,"cache_read_input_tokens":30935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1788,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyXu5PFchmbZXoAVrwn","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a3666826-87f0-41fe-94c3-4f0b48754644","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:54.443Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a3666826-87f0-41fe-94c3-4f0b48754644","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015nLSD25oxoeEHa9QUhqSNu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013srtLTAsk32b8YjYy9vy8D","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2508.11850","prompt":"Extract: 1) the exact prompt structure EvoCut uses to evolve MILP cuts, 2) how the LLM outputs cut formulas (Python? linear form?), 3) the evaluator metrics (solve time, gap, validity check), 4) how invalid/cutting-off-feasible cuts are detected and rejected, 5) how multiple cuts are combined."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1269,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1788,"cache_read_input_tokens":30935,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1788,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyXu5PFchmbZXoAVrwn","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e2f84f5e-f988-4a50-8068-ecb94f402c20","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:11:57.234Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
