{"parentUuid":"ef96267f-cb85-4e58-90d2-1d17db3e4f8e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d8b963fa-dadc-413b-9392-667bd1294b0d","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RyDAFoeHYZvdoLRKTF8QSf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"FunSearch reward hacking evaluator side effects LLM generated code sandboxing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reward Hacking in Reinforcement Learning | Lil'Log\",\"url\":\"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2024-11-28-reward-hacking/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - lumi-a/funsearch: Implementation of Google DeepMind's FunSearch\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lumi-a/funsearch\"},{\"title\":\"Reward Hacking Benchmark: Measuring Exploits in LLM Agents with Tool Use\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2605.02964\"},{\"title\":\"LLM Hacking: Techniques, Risks, and Mitigations\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/llm-hacking\"},{\"title\":\"NATURAL EMERGENT MISALIGNMENT FROM REWARD HACKING IN PRODUCTION RL\",\"url\":\"https://assets.anthropic.com/m/74342f2c96095771/original/Natural-emergent-misalignment-from-reward-hacking-paper.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Spontaneous Reward Hacking in Iterative Self-Refinement\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/papers/2407.04549\"},{\"title\":\"Reward Hacking: The Hidden Failure Mode in AI Optimization | by Adnan Masood, PhD. | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@adnanmasood/reward-hacking-the-hidden-failure-mode-in-ai-optimization-686b62acf408\"},{\"title\":\"Reward Hacking in Large Language Models (LLMs) | by Deepak Babu Piskala | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@prdeepak.babu/reward-hacking-in-large-language-models-llms-c57abbc0cde7\"},{\"title\":\"Can We Use AI to Discover Better Algorithms? | Richard Cornelius Suwandi\",\"url\":\"https://richardcsuwandi.github.io/blog/2025/llm-algorithm-discovery/\"},{\"title\":\"Reward hacking - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reward_hacking\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding FunSearch, reward hacking, evaluator side effects, LLM-generated code, and sandboxing:\n\n## FunSearch Overview\n\nFunSearch is a method introduced by Google DeepMind that demonstrates LLMs can make new discoveries in mathematical sciences by searching for novel \"functions\" written in computer code. FunSearch tackles the trade-off between LLMs' creativity and correctness by pairing a pre-trained LLM with an automated \"evaluator\" that guards against hallucinations and incorrect ideas.\n\n## Reward Hacking and Evaluator Issues\n\nUsing LLMs as evaluators or graders for feedback and training rewards is sometimes referred to as the \"LLM-as-grader paradigm,\" but this can introduce biases that can lead to reward hacking by exploiting these graders. Iterative self-refinement in LLMs can lead to reward hacking, where the evaluator's ratings improve while generation quality remains stagnant or even decreases as judged by actual user preference.\n\n## Code Sandboxing Concerns\n\nRegarding code execution safety, the code generated by the LLM is executed in a sandbox, which defaults to running the code on your system and offers no protection from malicious code. If you have Docker or Podman, you can pass --sandbox-type ContainerSandbox for safer sandboxing.\n\n## Side Effects and Advanced Threats\n\nContemporary reasoning models such as OpenAI's O1 series and DeepSeek-R1 have been found to reason about testing processes and take actions to maximize scores, with some models attempting to hack game systems by deleting or modifying their opponent's chess engine.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ccba30bc-df7e-4dce-af6c-bd5ac0bc1e56","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:12:07.157Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ef96267f-cb85-4e58-90d2-1d17db3e4f8e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e2f84f5e-f988-4a50-8068-ecb94f402c20","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d8b963fa-dadc-413b-9392-667bd1294b0d","agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013srtLTAsk32b8YjYy9vy8D","type":"tool_result","content":"# EvoCut: MILP Cut Generation Architecture\n\n## 1. Prompt Structure for Evolution\n\nEvoCut employs **three agent types** with specialized prompts:\n\n- **Initializer Agent**: Receives the complete MILP formulation code, natural language problem description, and instructions to \"propose novel and distinct acceleration cuts that tighten the LP relaxation\"\n- **Crossover Agent**: Merges features from two parent cuts to produce offspring\n- **Mutation Agent**: Alters coefficients or terms in a single parent cut\n\nThe paper states: *\"The complete prompt templates are provided in Appendix B\"* but the main text indicates agents receive \"(1) the code of the complete MILP formulation alongside a natural language description of all model components, (2) the set of cuts generated so far, and (3) explicit instructions.\"\n\n## 2. Cut Output Format\n\nLLM outputs are **executable Python code** (Pyomo modeling language):\n\nThe framework requires each response to include *\"a brief description (an idea) of the proposed cut together with executable code (e.g., Pyomo)\"*. The cut is formally represented as: **C := {A'ᵣx + G'ᵣy + H'ᵣz ≤ δᵣ}ᵣ∈ᵣ** where auxiliary variables z encode additional logical relations.\n\n## 3. Evaluator Metrics\n\n**Primary evaluation occurs in two phases:**\n\n**Verification Phase (must pass):**\n- Code compilation check\n- Optimal Solution Screening (OSS): Ensures reference solutions remain feasible on verification set Dᵥ\n- Usefulness check: Confirms cut separates ≥1 stored LP relaxation solution\n\n**Fitness Evaluation** (on evaluation set Dₑ):\nThe paper notes: *\"The key intuition is that a cut should receive higher fitness when it reduces the gap on average\"*. Fitness uses \"signed relative gap change per instance, averaging over Dₑ, and then applying a monotone mapping\" (details in Appendix H).\n\n## 4. Invalid Cut Detection & Rejection\n\n**Three failure modes trigger rejection and LLM retry (max 3 attempts):**\n\n1. **Code Check Failure**: *\"If a syntax or runtime error occurs, we return the error message to the generator agent for revision\"*\n\n2. **OSS Violation**: For each instance i ∈ Dᵥ, the system fixes original variables to stored optimal solutions (x̂*ᵢ, ŷ*ᵢ) and checks if there exists z satisfying the cut constraints. *\"If the reduced model is infeasible, C fails the OSS check\"*\n\n3. **Usefulness Failure**: *\"We retain C iff there exists i ∈ Dᵥ such that ∄z with A'ᵣx^LP_i + G'ᵣy^LP_i + H'ᵣz ≤ δᵣ\"* (i.e., cut must separate at least one fractional LP solution)\n\nThe post-hoc validation in Section 5.3 adds offline confirmation: *\"we fix the original decision variables to the proven optimal solution, append the learned cut, and solve only for any auxiliary variables\"*.\n\n## 5. Combining Multiple Cuts\n\nThe paper addresses **single-cut deployment only**: *\"We compare the baseline MILP to the baseline MILP augmented with a single EvoCut cut under fixed solver budgets.\"*\n\nNo mechanism for combining multiple cuts is discussed. The evolutionary process selects the highest-fitness single cut for test deployment, though population-level strategies could theoretically extend this (not explored in current work)."}]},"uuid":"6d35b5d4-8e1b-4929-909d-59e2e5b29177","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:12:09.755Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2f84f5e-f988-4a50-8068-ecb94f402c20","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6d35b5d4-8e1b-4929-909d-59e2e5b29177","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a08591c75ba641e6e","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01YG9kZTsXNW63w9iJdny9TQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me write the response.\n\n# 演化优化算法启发式 调研报告\n\n## 1. FunSearch bin packing 范式（priority function）\n\n**种子程序**（最简单，故意写得很烂，让 LLM 演化）：\n```python\n@funsearch.evolve\ndef priority(item: float, bins: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"对每个 bin 给一个分数，分数最高的 bin 接收 item。\"\"\"\n    return -(bins - item)  # 朴素 best-fit\n\n@funsearch.run\ndef evaluate(instances: dict) -> float:\n    \"\"\"跑所有 instance，返回 -avg(num_bins / lower_bound)。越大越好。\"\"\"\n    ...\n```\n\n**关键约定**：\n- `@funsearch.evolve` 标记**唯一**被改写的函数；其他代码冻结\n- `@funsearch.run` 是评估入口，返回**单个 float**（FunSearch 只看标量适应度）\n- Evaluator 内部用 OR3 (20 instances × 500 items, cap=150) + Weibull 5k (5 × 5000, cap=100)\n- 失败保护：调用前 syntax check + 沙箱执行 + 超时 + 数值 NaN/Inf 拒绝\n\n**Prompt 模板**（核心创新——multi-shot from database）：\n- 从 island 数据库中按分数加权采样 **k=2 个父程序** v0、v1\n- 拼成代码文件，函数名重命名为 `priority_v0`、`priority_v1`\n- 让 LLM 续写 `def priority_v2`，没有自然语言指令——纯代码续写\n\n## 2. AlphaEvolve SEARCH/REPLACE\n\n**演化区域标记**：\n```python\n# EVOLVE-BLOCK-START\ndef heuristic(...):\n    ...\n# EVOLVE-BLOCK-END\n```\n块外代码（imports、evaluator、I/O）冻结。\n\n**Diff 输出格式**（LLM 必须严格遵守）：\n```\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\nsearch text\n=======\nreplace text\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```\n\n**Prompt 包含**：父程序完整代码、最近 N 个 sibling 的 (代码片段, 分数)、evaluator 文本反馈、meta-prompt（自演化的指令）、elite + diverse 混合采样。\n\n## 3. OpenEvolve 配置三件套\n\n**目录**：\n```\nproject/\n  initial_program.py   # 含 EVOLVE-BLOCK\n  evaluator.py         # 函数 evaluate(program_path) -> dict\n  config.yaml\n```\n\n**evaluator.py 返回**：`{\"combined_score\": float, \"performance\": ..., \"correctness\": ...}` 或 `EvaluationResult(metrics=..., artifacts=...)`（artifacts 把 stderr/traceback 喂给下一轮 prompt，关键反馈机制）。\n\n**config.yaml**：\n```yaml\nmax_iterations: 1000\nllm:\n  models: [{name: \"gemini-2.0-flash\", weight: 0.7}, {name: \"gemini-2.0-pro\", weight: 0.3}]\n  temperature: 0.7\ndatabase:\n  population_size: 500\n  num_islands: 5            # MAP-Elites + 环形迁移\nevaluator:\n  enable_artifacts: true    # stderr 反馈\n  cascade_evaluation: true  # 三阶段过滤\n  use_llm_feedback: true\n```\n\n**Cascade 三阶段**：S1 syntax/import → S2 小数据 smoke test → S3 完整 benchmark。每阶段有阈值，过不了不进下一阶段。\n\n**入口**：`python openevolve-run.py initial_program.py evaluator.py --config config.yaml --iterations 1000`\n\n## 4. 怎么演化\"cut\"而不是 ranking 函数 —— EvoCut 范式\n\n**关键洞察**（EvoCut, arxiv 2508.11850）：cut 不是单一函数，而是**Pyomo 代码片段**：\n- LLM 输出：自然语言 idea + `def add_cut(model): model.cut = pyo.Constraint(...)` 可执行代码\n- 三 agent 分工：**Initializer**（从零生成）/**Crossover**（合并两个父 cut）/**Mutation**（改系数/项）\n- 验证三关：(a) 代码能跑 (b) **OSS 检查**：把已知最优解代入，cut 必须保持可行（防止切掉最优）(c) **usefulness**：至少切掉一个 LP 松弛分数解\n- 失败 → 错误消息回喂 LLM，最多 retry 3 次\n- Fitness = 平均相对 gap 缩减\n\n**对应到我们项目**：把 `# EVOLVE-BLOCK` 包在 `master_model.py` 里某个 `def add_symmetry_cut(model, ...)` 上，让 LLM 演化结构性 cut。\n\n## 5. Evaluator 必返 metric 清单（综合）\n\n| 字段 | 用途 |\n|------|------|\n| `combined_score` | 单值适应度（必需） |\n| `feasibility` (0/1) | 通过 OSS / 不切掉已知解 |\n| `runtime_seconds` | 时间预算监控 |\n| `lp_gap` / `dual_bound` | cut 类任务核心 |\n| `text_feedback` | 喂下一轮 prompt 的自然语言总结 |\n| `artifacts.stderr` | 错误回喂 |\n| `private` | 隐藏指标，防 LLM 看见后过拟合 |\n\n## 6. 失败模式 + 预防\n\n| 失败 | 预防 |\n|------|------|\n| 无意义代码（pass / return 0） | 种子程序非平凡 + cascade S1 拒绝低于种子分数的 |\n| 作弊（硬编码 instance 答案、读评估文件、import 外部解算器结果） | evaluator **私有持有 hidden test set**；沙箱禁网络/文件 IO；evaluator 用 hash 校验输入未被改 |\n| 切掉最优解（cut 类） | **OSS check**：每次新 cut 用已知最优解 verify |\n| 数值不稳（NaN/Inf/超时） | 超时 kill + NaN 检测 + 拒绝；ShinkaEvolve 用 `r^u = exp(max(r-r_b, 0))-1` 防 reward 非平稳作弊 |\n| 雷同程序灌库 | ShinkaEvolve novelty rejection：embedding cosine > 0.95 → LLM 二次确认 → 重采 |\n| 修改 immutable 区 | 解析时强制 EVOLVE-BLOCK 边界，违规直接拒 + reflexion 反馈 |\n\n---\n\n## 给项目的 1 周 PoC 完整框架（演化 master_model 对称破缺 cut）\n\n**目标**：让 LLM 演化 `add_symmetry_breaking_cut(model, candidates)`，目标函数 = 平均 LP gap 缩减 × 求解时间惩罚。\n\n**目录**：`D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\experiments\\alphaevolve_poc\\`\n\n**initial_program.py**：\n```python\nimport pyomo.environ as pyo\nimport numpy as np\n\n# EVOLVE-BLOCK-START\ndef add_symmetry_cut(model, candidates: list, mandatory_count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    给 master_model 加结构性 cut，返回添加的 cut 数。\n    候选信息：candidates[i] = {\"x\":int,\"y\":int,\"w\":int,\"h\":int,\"facility\":str}\n    禁止：删除已有约束、修改目标、读外部文件。\n    \"\"\"\n    # 朴素种子：lex 序破缺同型设施\n    n = 0\n    by_type = {}\n    for i, c in enumerate(candidates):\n        by_type.setdefault(c[\"facility\"], []).append(i)\n    for typ, idxs in by_type.items():\n        for a, b in zip(idxs, idxs[1:]):\n            model.add_component(f\"sym_{typ}_{a}_{b}\",\n                pyo.Constraint(expr=model.x[a] >= model.x[b]))\n            n += 1\n    return n\n# EVOLVE-BLOCK-END\n```\n\n**evaluator.py**：\n```python\nfrom openevolve import EvaluationResult\nimport subprocess, json, time, hashlib\n\nHIDDEN_INSTANCES = [\"valley4_seed_001.json\",\"valley4_seed_017.json\", ...]  # 私有\nKNOWN_OPTIMAL = json.load(open(\"data/preprocessed/known_optima.json\"))\n\ndef evaluate(program_path):\n    # Stage 1: import & syntax\n    try:\n        spec = __import__(program_path); fn = spec.add_symmetry_cut\n    except Exception as e:\n        return EvaluationResult(metrics={\"combined_score\":-1e9},\n                                artifacts={\"stderr\":str(e),\"stage\":\"S1\"})\n    # Stage 2: smoke (10s budget, 1 small instance)\n    smoke = run_solver(fn, \"smoke_5x5.json\", timeout=10)\n    if not smoke[\"feasible\"]:\n        return EvaluationResult(metrics={\"combined_score\":-1e6},\n                                artifacts={\"stderr\":\"smoke infeasible\",\"stage\":\"S2\"})\n    # Stage 3: OSS - cut 不能切掉已知最优\n    for inst, opt in KNOWN_OPTIMAL.items():\n        if cuts_off_optimum(fn, inst, opt):\n            return EvaluationResult(metrics={\"combined_score\":-1e7,\"oss_violated\":1},\n                                    artifacts={\"stderr\":f\"cut removes optimum {inst}\"})\n    # Stage 4: full benchmark on hidden set\n    gaps, times = [], []\n    for inst in HIDDEN_INSTANCES:\n        r = run_solver(fn, inst, timeout=60)\n        gaps.append(r[\"lp_gap_reduction\"]); times.append(r[\"wall_seconds\"])\n    score = float(np.mean(gaps)) - 0.01*float(np.mean(times))\n    return EvaluationResult(\n        metrics={\"combined_score\":score,\n                 \"avg_gap_reduction\":float(np.mean(gaps)),\n                 \"avg_seconds\":float(np.mean(times)),\n                 \"feasibility\":1.0},\n        artifacts={\"text_feedback\":\n                   f\"gap reduced {np.mean(gaps):.3f}, time {np.mean(times):.1f}s\"})\n```\n\n**config.yaml**：\n```yaml\nmax_iterations: 200          # 1 周预算\nllm:\n  models:\n    - {name: \"claude-opus-4-7\", weight: 0.5}\n    - {name: \"gemini-2.5-pro\",  weight: 0.5}\n  temperature: 0.8\ndatabase:\n  population_size: 80\n  num_islands: 4\n  parent_selection_strategy: \"weighted\"   # ShinkaEvolve 风格\n  exploitation_alpha: 1.0\nevaluator:\n  enable_artifacts: true\n  cascade_evaluation: true\n  cascade_thresholds: [-1e8, -1e3, 0.0]   # S1/S2/S3 门槛\n  use_llm_feedback: false                  # PoC 阶段先关，避免双 LLM 串环\n  novelty_threshold: 0.95                  # embedding 拒绝雷同\n  timeout_seconds: 90\nprompt:\n  system: |\n    You are improving a CP-SAT master model symmetry-breaking cut for a 70x70\n    placement problem. CRITICAL RULES:\n    1) Never modify code outside EVOLVE-BLOCK markers.\n    2) Cuts must be valid: they cannot remove any feasible optimal placement.\n    3) Output only SEARCH/REPLACE diff blocks. No prose outside diffs.\n    4) Prefer cuts that reduce LP gap with minimal added constraints.\n```\n\n**安全契约对齐项目 CLAUDE.md**：\n- evaluator 写在 `experiments/alphaevolve_poc/`，**不碰** `data/checkpoints/`、`data/solutions/`、`data/blueprints/`\n- LLM 产出永远是 **hint/order_only**，不进 certified proof source\n- HIDDEN_INSTANCES 不在 prompt 里出现 → LLM 看不见 → 不能过拟合\n- KNOWN_OPTIMAL OSS check 是**硬墙**：违反直接 -1e7，不可能演化出\"作弊但分高\"的 cut\n\n**1 周节奏**：\n- D1：写 evaluator + 跑通 smoke\n- D2：5 个 hidden instance + OSS oracle\n- D3-D5：跑 200 iterations，每天 ultrareview 顶 5 个 cut\n- D6：把最佳 cut 在 **完整 70x70 campaign** 上 shadow 跑（不写 checkpoint）\n- D7：写 PoC 报告 + 决定是否进 Phase 3B 主线\n\nSources:\n- [FunSearch GitHub](https://github.com/google-deepmind/funsearch)\n- [FunSearch bin packing notebook](https://github.com/google-deepmind/funsearch/blob/main/bin_packing/bin_packing.ipynb)\n- [FunSearch Nature paper PDF](https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/DeepMind.com/Blog/funsearch-making-new-discoveries-in-mathematical-sciences-using-large-language-models/Mathematical-discoveries-from-program-search-with-large-language-models.pdf)\n- [AlphaEvolve DeepMind blog](https://deepmind.google/blog/alphaevolve-a-gemini-powered-coding-agent-for-designing-advanced-algorithms/)\n- [AlphaEvolve getting started (TDS)](https://towardsdatascience.com/googles-alphaevolve-getting-started-with-evolutionary-coding-agents/)\n- [OpenEvolve GitHub](https://github.com/algorithmicsuperintelligence/openevolve)\n- [OpenEvolve overview](https://algorithmicsuperintelligence.ai/blog/openevolve-overview/index.html)\n- [ShinkaEvolve paper (arxiv 2509.19349)](https://arxiv.org/html/2509.19349v1)\n- [ShinkaEvolve GitHub](https://github.com/SakanaAI/ShinkaEvolve)\n- [EvoCut: MILP cut evolution (arxiv 2508.11850)](https://arxiv.org/html/2508.11850)\n- [CodeEvolve framework (arxiv 2510.14150)](https://arxiv.org/html/2510.14150v4)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1384,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2848,"cache_read_input_tokens":32723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2848,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoyZjZSsLK2kWXhgW3XC","attributionAgent":"gener